 "unknowns": [
  {
   "configuration_id": "cryofab_cmsh100_vented_bath",
   "key": "temperature.range",
   "why": "Rejected because the source does not apply to this model. The quote is from the NIST NCNR Orange cryostat page and describes Orange cryostats' warm-valve exhaust, not the Cryofab CMSH 100. Cryofab's own CMSH manual only says LHe at atmospheric pressure is 'approximately -452°F', which is about 4.26 K. The manual also says nothing about dip-probe use, and its RV-3 pressure control valve (0.5 PSI) means the closed dewar runs slightly above 1 atm. Re-source from the Cryofab manual (about 4.26 K) or use NIST LHe reference data at 1 atm (4.22 K, i.e. 4222 mK, not 4200)."
  },
  {
   "configuration_id": "cryofab_cmsh100_vented_bath",
   "key": "temperature.base",
   "why": "Rejected for the same reason: a cross-instrument source (NIST Orange cryostat page). 4.2 K also slightly overstates how cold the bath gets; normal boiling point is 4.22 K, and Cryofab gives about -452°F, roughly 4.26 K."
  }
 ],
